# Grammar calls a noun made from a verb a nominalization (`decision`
# from `decide`). Each phrase is a weak verb plus a noun that names the
# real verb (`make a decision`, `perform a lookup`, `take into
# account`), or a form of `be` plus an adjective that does the same (`is
# dependent on`). The list names each phrase in full, because a pattern
# such as `[make, perform] DET NOUN` also matches `make a copy` and
# `perform the request`, where the noun is the object and no single verb
# replaces the pair.
#
# Each verb carries its forms for tense and person. `$perform` expands
# to perform, performs, performed, and performing through Harper's
# dictionary, and the lists below add what the dictionary leaves out,
# such as `made`, `took`, and `drew`. `provide` lists its forms by hand,
# because `$provide` also matches `provider` (`provider support for
# Kubernetes`).
#
# `make a request` and `gain access to` sit in the Recommended rule of
# the same name.
expr make [$make, made]
expr take [$take, taking, took, taken]
expr give [$give, gave, given]
expr provide [provide, provides, provided, providing]
expr have [has, have, had, having]
expr be [is, are, was, were]
expr main [(@make [(a decision), decisions, (a choice), (a comparison), (an assumption), (an attempt), (use of), (a determination), (a distinction), (a selection), (a call to)]), ($perform [(a check), validation, (a lookup), (an update), (an analysis), (a search), (a comparison)]), (@take [(a look), action, (into consideration), (into account)]), (@give [consideration, (an indication), (a description of)]), (@provide [(support for), (a description of)]), (@be in charge of), ($conduct [(a review), (an analysis)]), ($carry out), ([do, does, did, doing] a comparison), (@have [(an effect on), (an impact on), (a need for)]), ($reach a decision), ([$come, came] to a conclusion), ([$draw, drew, drawn] a conclusion), (@be [(indicative of), (reflective of), (dependent on), (dependent upon), (reliant on)]), (in need of), ([$put, putting] emphasis on), ($place emphasis on), (@be of [importance, significance, use])]
let message "Nominalization. Use the verb."
let description "Flags a weak verb plus noun where one verb does the work."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The decoder makes a copy of the buffer before it writes."
allows "The client performs the request and returns the body."
allows "Set decides which bucket receives the token."
allows "Provider support for Kubernetes varies by cloud."
